# HR-4D Red OpenPAI Training Commands

This note records the offline training commands for the HR-4D radar setup when the raw data root and the PKL directory are separated.

## Paths

Raw data root:

```bash
/mnt/nas_02
```

PKL directory:

```bash
/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend
```

Train PKLs:

```bash
infos_train.pkl
infos_train_bad_demotion.pkl
```

Test PKLs:

```bash
infos_test.pkl
infos_rainy.pkl
```

The current `RadarDataset` resolves `INFO_PATH` entries as:

- absolute path: use directly
- relative path: resolve relative to `DATA_CONFIG.DATA_PATH`

For this setup, use absolute PKL paths and keep `DATA_CONFIG.DATA_PATH` pointing at the raw radar data root.

## Single-GPU Training

Run from the repository `tools` directory:

```bash
cd /workspace/4DRadar/tools

CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python train.py \
  --cfg_file cfgs/radar_models/pointpillar_radar.yaml \
  --epochs 40 \
  --batch_size 8 \
  --workers 8 \
  --logger_iter_interval 100 \
  --extra_tag offline_sep_paths_ep40 \
  --set \
  DATA_CONFIG.DATA_PATH /mnt/nas_02 \
  DATA_CONFIG.INFO_PATH.train "['/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend/infos_train.pkl','/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend/infos_train_bad_demotion.pkl']" \
  DATA_CONFIG.INFO_PATH.test "['/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend/infos_test.pkl','/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend/infos_rainy.pkl']"
```

## Multi-GPU Training

For 8 GPUs, use `torchrun`:

```bash
cd /workspace/4DRadar/tools

CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 torchrun \
  --nproc_per_node=8 \
  train.py \
  --launcher pytorch \
  --cfg_file cfgs/radar_models/pointpillar_radar.yaml \
  --epochs 40 \
  --batch_size 16 \
  --workers 8 \
  --logger_iter_interval 100 \
  --extra_tag offline_sep_paths_8gpu_ep40 \
  --set \
  DATA_CONFIG.DATA_PATH /mnt/nas_02 \
  DATA_CONFIG.INFO_PATH.train "['/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend/infos_train.pkl','/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend/infos_train_bad_demotion.pkl']" \
  DATA_CONFIG.INFO_PATH.test "['/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend/infos_test.pkl','/mnt/nas/train/usr/meng.sun3/pkls/radar/LRR610/202606_12W_extend/infos_rainy.pkl']"
```

In this repository, `--batch_size` is the total batch size across all GPUs.

Example:

- `--batch_size 16` with 8 GPUs means batch size 2 per GPU
- `--batch_size 32` with 8 GPUs means batch size 4 per GPU

## Optional AMP

If you want mixed precision, add:

```bash
--use_amp
```

## Notes

- These commands assume the sample paths stored inside each PKL can be resolved relative to `/mnt/nas_02`.
- If the paths inside the PKLs point to another root, `DATA_CONFIG.DATA_PATH` must be changed to that actual root.
- For the first verification run, it is safer to reduce batch size or run fewer epochs before launching the full training job.
